# PART 11 — ROW LEVEL SECURITY (RLS)

Enable Row Level Security on all tables that contain protected application data.

Policies must ensure:

Public visitors:
- Can read active categories.
- Can read published products.
- Can read public product descriptions and public product image metadata.
- Cannot read private file object keys.
- Cannot read customer profiles.
- Cannot read private download history.
- Cannot read admin logs.
- Cannot modify products or categories.

Authenticated customers:
- Can read and update only their own permitted profile fields.
- Can read their own download history.
- Cannot read other customers' records.
- Cannot grant themselves product access.
- Cannot change their role.
- Cannot access admin functions.

Administrators:
- Can perform authorized management actions.
- Must be validated through a secure role check.
- Must not rely only on frontend route protection.

Important:
Never rely only on hiding admin pages in the frontend. Enforce authorization in the database and backend APIs.

Use the Supabase service role key only in trusted server-side environments. Never put it in a `VITE_` variable or expose it in browser bundles.

